On Wed, Dec 14, 2011 at 5:42 PM, Robin Lee Powell
<rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org> wrote:
> I read it as "x1 does x2 every x3".
>
> On Wed, Dec 14, 2011 at 12:39:24PM -0800, ianek wrote:
>> x1 is regular/cyclical/periodic in property (ka)/activity x2 with
>> period/interval x3.
>> Actor is periodic? And there is a suggestion that x2 is a property
>> related to being periodic, whatever it means.

x1 can but need not be an actor, depending on what role it plays in property x2:

mi dikni lo ka ce'u re roi klama lo zarci kei lo jeftu be li pa
"I regularly go twice to the market every week."

There the x1 is the actor because "lo ka ce'u re roi klama lo zarci"
is an actor's property, but:

lo zarci cu dikni lo ka mi re roi klama ce'u kei lo jeftu be li pa
"The market is regularly gone to twice by me every week."

Now the property is not the property of an actor, so x1 is not an actor.

x1 is something that has property x2 every x3.

